{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST Event Translation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST Event Translation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ghost event translation blender ghost event translation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST Event Translation.md","fileName":"Blender GHOST Event Translation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender GHOST Event Translation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Operator and Event System]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Window Event Queue","Blender GHOST Event Consumer","Blender Event Distribution Pipeline","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST Event Translation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST Event Translation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ghost event translation blender ghost event translation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST Event Translation.md","fileName":"Blender GHOST Event Translation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender GHOST Event Translation","heading":"Blender GHOST Event Translation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender's GHOST callback receives portable low-level event types and converts them into application-level work. Window concerns such as opening a file can invoke a registered operator directly, while mouse, key, cursor, and similar input is translated into a Blender event record.\n\nTranslation assigns Blender-specific codes, values, coordinates, and custom data before adding the result to a [[Blender Window Event Queue]]. This is the bridge between the [[Blender GHOST Event Consumer]] and the higher [[Blender Event Distribution Pipeline]].","tags":["baby"],"